{"hookSpecificOutput":{"additionalContext":"Grid tracks tasks, Jobs and shared knowledge in one Grid home.\nGRID_HOME is the Grid data folder ~/.grid; GRID_PROJECTS is ~/.grid/projects.\nGrid project: ideas, folder <ROOT>/notes/ideas. It has no Grid record yet; the first task makes one.\nTask files live under the Grid home; use the grid verbs for task.md, the plan, the history and Jobs, and write any other task file straight into its folder. Project records and task files live outside repositories.\nThe Grid brain holds shared topics, knowledge and decisions at home and project level.\nApprovals come from a person through the Grid app or grid approve in a terminal outside Claude Code or Codex.\nBrain: project knowledge first, then home knowledge.\ntopic | description | entries | last_change | invalid\ndecisions | Decisions and their reasons | 0 | - | 0\nconventions | Project practices and lessons | 0 | - | 0\nenvironments | Development and test settings | 0 | - | 0\nmachines | Computers and capacity | 0 | - | 0\ndeploy | Delivery targets and steps | 0 | - | 0\npeople | Members and approvers | 0 | - | 0\nagents | Agent settings | 0 | - | 0\nroutines | Scheduled work | 0 | - | 0\nRead a note: grid brain search --topic \u003ctopic\u003e \u003cwords\u003e, then grid brain show \u003cid\u003e.\n\nGrid has no config and no data on this computer yet. Offer the person once to run the grid:first-run skill, and carry on with their request if they decline.","hookEventName":"SessionStart"},"systemMessage":"Grid is not set up on this computer yet. Run /grid:first-run to set it up; it takes a minute."}
